      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "is to his mate. In order to secure the elephant, there must be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "a strong post (आलान ); and to curb a sensual mind a strong",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "control or restraint. The post and the restraint, the elephant",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "and the mind and the sensual objects and the female elephant,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "are the pairs compared here. तादृक्—a worldly man who is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "strong minded enough to resist the temptation of sensual",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "objects. क्षीब—intoxicated. आलान a post for fastening elephants.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 83. अकार्पण्य—cf. कृपणां वृत्तिं Nit. sl. 49. उपशम—tranquil-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "lity, or peace of mind, subduing the passions entirely. बहिः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "मन्दस्पन्दम्—( the mind too ), moving ( but ) slowly towards",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "external objects. The mind is solely engaged in contemplation",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "and hardly bestows any thought on external objects. The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "internal objects for a comtemplative mind are itself and the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "supreme soul; while the entire creation constitutes outer",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "things. These latter are referred to by the word बहिस्.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 84. जीर्णाः—have died out. Cf. जीर्णमङ्गे सुभाषितम् Sl. 2.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "वन्ध्यफलतां याताः—have become sterile, have borne no fruit.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "कृतान्तः-see com.; or कृतं अन्तयतीति. अक्षमी—unforgiving, unrelent-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "ing; क्षमा विद्यते अस्य क्षमी न क्षमी अक्षमी. ह्याज्ञातम्—v. l. = हि + आ +",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ज्ञातम्, आ being taken स्मरणे as Mr. Talang suggests. But here",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "हि has no propriety.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 85. मे भेदप्रतिपत्तिर्नास्ति—I see no difference; I have no",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "idea of difference between &c. प्रतिपत्ति—knowledge, idea.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "जगताम्—the plural is used because according to the Hindu",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "notion there are 14 worlds.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 86. पुलिने—तोयोत्थितं तत्पुलिनं Amara; a sandy bank left",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "by receding water; goes with द्युसरितः. द्युसरित्—the heavenly river,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the Ganges. भवाभोगोद्विग्नाः—बहुदुःखजन्मपरंपराभीताः Rámarshi; cf.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "शमसुखाभोग sl. 96 infra. आत्तवचसः v. l.—आत्तं गृहीतं वचः यैः ते;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "who have taken to ( i. e. are repeating ) the words. आनन्दोद्भूत",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "&c.—Bah. The joy referred to is, of course, that resulting",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "from the manifestation of the Supreme Deity in contempla-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "tion. आर्तवचसः v. l. is meaningless unless we take it to mean",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "' earnest cries, fervent prayers, ' ( आर्तस्य इव वचः येषां ).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
